; layouts/split-year-assert — the tree an import cannot be reckoned inside.
;
; THIS file is the journal. `2026/2026.journal` is a FRAGMENT of it, and the
; fragment's first transaction asserts the balance 2025 closed with — so it is
; correct here and cannot be correct anywhere else:
;
;   $ hledger -f main.journal check         # passes; the tree is fine
;   $ hledger -f 2026/2026.journal check    # FAILS, and nothing is wrong
;
; Both halves of that are the point. An assertion inside an included fragment is
; not a check we choose to switch off during an import; it is a check that is
; structurally incapable of being correct when only the fragment is read,
; because the balance it asserts accumulates through a file hledger was never
; asked to open. See `import_api::import_invocation` and `verify_balance`.
;
; Balances for `assets:bank:checking`, which the tests pin:
;
;   through this file      $895.00     ($1,000.00 - $100.00 - $5.00)
;   2026/2026.journal alone  $-5.00
;
; Equality with the second number is the bug, which is why both are asserted.

account assets:bank:checking
account equity:opening balances
account expenses:food:coffee
account expenses:groceries
account expenses:home:rent
account income:salary

commodity $1,000.00

include 2025/2025.journal
include 2026/2026.journal
